 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to service award\nprograms",
    "basePrintNo": "S7315",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7315-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §219-d, Gen Muni L (as proposed in S. 899 and A. 6873)",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7315\n\nSPONSOR: CROCI\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the general municipal law, in relation\nto service award programs\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would provide for a three-way negotiated and agreed chapter\namendment for S.899\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nThe original bill, 5.899, would require a mandatory referendum any time\na volunteer ambulance service award program is amended to increase the\nnumber of points granted for an activity or if the amount of activity\nrequired to earn points is decreased. The original bill would further\nprovide that amendments to a service award program would only take\neffect as of the first of January next succeeding the adoption of the\namendment and prohibit retroactive amendments.  Lastly, the original\nbill would also authorize program sponsors of volunteer ambulance\nservice awards to lower the entitlement age for defined benefit service\naward programs to fifty-five.\n\nThis chapter amendment would change the section reference for the enti-\ntlement age section of the bill from section 219 m of the general munic-\nipal law to 219 e of the general municipal law. Section 219 e relates to\nparticipation, vesting and service credit for defined contribution\nservice award programs for volunteer ambulance workers, while section\n219 m relates to defined benefit service award programs for volunteer\nambulance workers.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would provide for a three-way negotiated and agreed chapter\namendment for 5.899 as set forth above.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone Noted.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act would take effect on the first of January next succeeding the\ndate on which it shall have become law (meaning January 1, 2018 as Chap-\nter 426 of the laws of 2017 was signed (S.899) on November 29, 2017).\n",
